      "symbol": "%",
      "name": "rem",
      "arity": 2,
      "associativity": "left",
      "category": "arithmetic",
      "source": "sbml-core",
      "attested": true,
      "note": "Infix form of rem(x, y), as in libsbml's L3 infix parser with its L3v2 modulo setting. Same precedence as * and /, left-associative. The result has the sign of the dividend (x - y*trunc(x/y)): -7 % 3 is -1, not 2. That matches C++ fmod and Java's %, but NOT Python's %, which follows the divisor's sign - the Python library must evaluate it with math.fmod."
    },
