        "min": 1,
        "max": null
      },
      "category": "conditional",
      "source": "sbml-core",
      "attested": true,
      "note": "libsbml's argument order: piecewise(value1, condition1, value2, condition2, ..., otherwise). Each value comes before its condition, matching MathML's <piece>. The trailing unpaired argument is the 'otherwise' value and is optional. The first pair whose condition is true wins. With no otherwise and no true condition, the result is undefined (NaN). Note that condition-first order would parse the same way, so the order cannot be checked; examples and docs should always show value-first."
    }
