  "notes": {
    "scope": "Registers every name usable inside SED2 infix math: the SBML Level 3 Core MathML subset (operators, call-style functions, constants - sbml-specifications/sbml-level-3/version-2/core/spec/preliminary.tex, sec:mathmlsubset), all 12 SBML distrib package csymbol draw functions (sbml-level-3/version-1/distrib/sbml-level-3-distrib-package-proposal.tex, tab:csymbols), and sum, the one SED2-specific extension attested in the spec's own example text.",
    "excluded-csymbols": "SBML's other core csymbols - time, delay(x,d), avogadro, rateOf(x) - are deliberately NOT registered here. They describe quantities internal to a running SBML model simulation (current integration time, a model rate rule's derivative, etc.), not SED2-level task outputs, and the SED2 spec's own inventory ('the functions allowed in SBML' / 'the constants allowed in SBML (pi, exponentiale, etc.)') lines up with the plain MathML-subset token list, not this separate csymbol section. Revisit if a concrete SED2 use case needs one of them.",
    "distrib-bounds": "min is inclusive for every distribution. For continuous distributions max is exclusive; for discrete distributions (binomial, poisson) max is inclusive. Use INF/-INF for an unbounded side. (sbml-level-3-distrib-package-proposal.tex, sec:extended-math)",
    "infix-conventions": "Relational operators, logical operators, and piecewise follow libsbml's L3 infix parser (src/sbml/math/L3Parser.ypp): the symbols ==, !=, <, >, <=, >=, &&, ||, ! plus call forms eq(), neq(), lt(), gt(), leq(), geq(), and(), or(), xor(), not(), implies(); and piecewise(value, condition, ..., otherwise). Decided 2026-09-24; none of this appears in the SED2 source text, but the spec inherits 'the functions allowed in SBML', and matching libsbml means any formula libsbml accepts reads the same way in SED2. libsbml's % operator is adopted as infix rem(); its 'lambda' is not."
  }
}
